BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Department of Classics] Serena Connolly (Rutgers University–New
  Brunswick) "Hadrian the Intellectual\, Revisited"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T130000
DTSTAMP:20261030T182615Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53932172382823-53932172383848@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Talk description:\n\nScholars have long paid attention to the 
 emperor Hadrian’s philhellenism\, in particular his support for Greek ar
 ts and culture. His commitment to science and technology has been comparat
 ively neglected\, despite our considerable evidence. This paper seeks to r
 emedy that imbalance and will also argue for understanding Hadrian’s int
 erests in science and technology as inspired by not only personal predilec
 tion but also precedent stretching back to Augustus.\n\nShort Bio:\n\nSere
 na Con\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://classics.stanford.edu/events/all
 -upcoming-events\nLast synced: 2026-10-30 11:26 PDT
LOCATION:Building 110
URL:https://classics.stanford.edu/events/all-upcoming-events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[CREEES Center for Russian\, East European & Eurasian Studies / Pr
 ogram in International Relations] State-Building by Other Means: Selective
  Enforcement and the Capital of Impunity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T130000
DTSTAMP:20261030T182615Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53862178635754-53862178636779@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Most work on corruption assumes it is an exception: rules exis
 t\, most people follow them\, some do not. From that assumption follow the
  standard instruments — measure how much corruption there is\, design re
 forms to reduce the number of violations.\n\nThis talk is about places whe
 re that assumption does not hold. Breaking rules there is an ordinary cond
 ition of doing business. What is "corruption" in such a context\, once it 
 can no longer be described as a set of violations? Derrer’s research fin
 ds t\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-30 11:26 PDT
LOCATION:Encina Commons
END:VEVENT
